<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Wanjiku recorded the price of a cup of chai at <m>{36}</m> kiosks in Kisumu, and found the standard deviation. Her working has one mistake.</p><tabular border="1" style="border-collapse:collapse;text-align:center;"><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Price of a cup (Ksh, <m>x</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">10</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">15</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">20</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">25</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">30</cell></row><row><cell style="padding:4px 10px;">Number of kiosks (<m>f</m>)</cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{3}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{10}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{12}</m></cell><cell style="padding:4px 10px;"><m>{1}</m></cell></row></tabular><ol><li><m>\Sigma f = {36}</m></li><li><m>\Sigma fx = {710}</m></li><li><m>\Sigma fx^2 = {154300}</m></li><li><m>\bar{x} = {710} \div {36} \approx {19.722}</m></li><li><m>\sigma^2 = {154300} \div {36} - {388.966} \approx {3897.145}</m></li><li><m>\sigma \approx {62.43}</m></li></ol><p>(a) Which step has the mistake?</p><div>[ Step 1 | Step 2 | Step 3 | Step 4 | Step 5 | Step 6 ]  </div><p>(b) Give the correct standard deviation in shillings, correct to 2 decimal places.</p><div><m>\sigma =</m> <fillin characters="6" name="ans2"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Check each step against the method: <m>\sigma^2 = \dfrac{\Sigma fx^2}{\Sigma f} - \bar{x}^2</m> and <m>\sigma = \sqrt{\sigma^2}</m>. The variance is the mean of the squares minus the square of the mean, and the standard deviation is its square root, in the units of the data.</p><p>(a) The mistake is in Step 3. Wanjiku squared each <m>fx</m>. Each term should be <m>f \times x^2</m>, so <m>\Sigma fx^2 = {14950}</m>.</p><p>(b) <me>\sigma^2 = \frac{ {14950} }{ {36} } - \left(\frac{ {710} }{ {36} }\right)^2 \approx {26.312}, \qquad \sigma \approx {5.13}</me></p></p></solution>
    <answer><p>Step 3</p></answer>
    <answer><p><m>\frac{5 \sqrt{341}}{18}</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>